# Cross-platform line-ending normalization for the UAL-ClaudeWorkflow template repo.
#
# Default behavior: every text file lives in the repo with LF line endings.
# Git's autocrlf handles checkout on Windows clients (converts to CRLF on
# checkout, back to LF on commit). Eliminates the recurring "LF will be
# replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it" warnings on a cross-platform
# team (Windows + Linux + macOS clones all coexist cleanly).
#
# Platform-native exceptions: .bat + .cmd files MUST keep CRLF because cmd.exe
# refuses to execute LF-only batch scripts. .ps1 files keep CRLF as the
# Windows PowerShell native convention.
#
# Binary files are explicitly marked so Git doesn't try to text-normalize them.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts — keep CRLF
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary files — never normalize (Unity AI Lab atree binary etc.)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
atree binary
